<% content_for :title, "The eight architectures" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Eight architectures of the same shop: an annual report, a single document, a scroll choreography, a floor plan, a command line, a newspaper, a conversation, and a control room." %>

<%# The index of the eight. Not a world itself: the one page that explains the
    whole set, written in the default architecture's clothes. %>
<div class="inst">
  <header class="inst-run">
    <p class="inst-run__mark"><%= Store.name %></p>
    <p class="inst-run__section">The eight architectures</p>
    <p>Design note</p>
  </header>

  <div class="inst-body">
    <article class="inst-sheet inst-sheet--wide">
      <section class="inst-clause">
        <div class="inst-clause__head">
          <p class="inst-clause__number">&#167;</p>
          <h1 class="inst-clause__title">Eight kinds of website, one store.</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="inst-standing">
          These are not colourways. Each world disagrees about what a page is: how many pages
          there are, how you move between them, and what happens when you scroll. The records
          behind all eight are the same catalogue and the same library.
        </p>
        <p class="inst-note">
          The dock in the bottom-left corner of every page moves between them. This page is the
          index: what each one is, in one line.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="inst-clause">
        <ul class="inst-worlds">
          <% @worlds.each do |world| %>
            <li class="inst-world">
              <p class="inst-world__tagline"><%= world.tagline %></p>
              <p class="inst-world__name">
                <%= link_to world.name, world.home_path, class: "inst-reading-list__title" %>
              </p>
              <p class="inst-world__premise"><%= world.premise %></p>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="inst-clause">
        <div class="inst-clause__head">
          <p class="inst-clause__number">&#167;</p>
          <h2 class="inst-clause__title">What stays the same</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="inst-clause__standfirst">
          The cart, the checkout, the order, the account and the admin keep one sober design in
          every world. The checkout is its own system, and it should look like one.
        </p>
        <div class="inst-actions">
          <%= link_to "The catalogue", shop_path, class: "inst-link" %>
          <%= link_to "The library", learn_path, class: "inst-link" %>
          <%= link_to "Standards", page_path("standards"), class: "inst-link" %>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
